1
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:08,220
巴菲特先生，您曾说过，在座的大多数人
Mr. Buffett, you’ve indicated that most of us in this room

2
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:13,280
都能从年报中获得您和查理掌握的大量信息。
could acquire a lot of the information that you and Charlie acquire through the annual reports.

3
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:20,940
但您二位也说过，会计准则很多时候并不尽如人意。
Yet you both also indicated that the GAAP rules, a lot of times, leave a little to be desired.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,900
能否请您谈谈，您和查理是如何得出经济价值，
Could you perhaps give an indication as to how you and Charlie come up with the economic value,

5
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:31,560
也就是你们最终决定投资的那些企业的内在价值？
or the intrinsic value, of the businesses that you finally decide to invest in?

6
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:35,720
再讲讲你们这样做的过程？谢谢。
And a little bit about the process that you go through with that? Thank you.

7
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:42,040
嗯，我们在 1992 年的年报里对此讨论得不少。
Well, in the 1992 annual report, we discuss that a fair amount.

8
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:50,070
但任何资产的经济价值，本质上，
But the economic value of any asset, essentially,

9
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:55,060
就是按适当的利率折现后，
is the present value, the appropriate interest rate,

10
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:59,240
企业未来全部现金流入和流出的现值。
of all the future streams of cash going in or out of the business.

11
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:03,980
有各种各样的企业，查理和我
And there are all kinds of businesses that Charlie and I

12
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:08,460
觉得自己完全不知道它们未来的现金流会是什么样子。
don’t think we have the faintest idea what that future stream will look like.

13
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:11,200
而如果我们完全不知道未来的现金流会是什么样子，
And if we don’t have the faintest idea what the future stream is going to look like,

14
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:14,040
我们也就完全不知道它现在值多少钱。
we don’t have the faintest idea what it’s worth, now.

15
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:17,220
所以，如果你认为自己知道一只股票今天该值多少，
So, if you think you know what the price of a stock should be today,

16
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:21,460
却对它未来 20 年的现金流毫无概念，
but you don’t think you have any idea what the stream of cash will be over the next 20 years,

17
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:27,550
那你就有了所谓的“认知失调”吧。
you’ve got cognitive dissonance, I guess, is what they call it.

18
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:37,580
所以我们寻找的是这样的东西：我们有相当高的把握，
So we are looking for things where we feel — fairly high degree of probability —

19
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:42,720
能把未来一段时间里的这些数字，预测在一个区间之内，
that we can come within a range of looking at those numbers out over a period of time,

20
00:01:42,780 --> 00:01:44,320
然后再把它们折现回来。
and then we discount them back.

21
00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:50,240
我们更关心这些数字的确定性，
And we are more concerned with the certainty of those numbers

22
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:54,240
而不是去找那个看起来绝对最便宜、
than we are with getting the one that looks absolutely the cheapest,

23
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:59,960
却建立在我们并没有多大把握的数字之上的东西。
but based upon numbers that we don’t have any — we don’t have great confidence in.

24
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:02,620
这基本上就是经济价值的全部含义。
And that’s basically what economic value is all about.

25
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:10,640
任何会计报告里的数字，本身都不代表经济价值。
The numbers in any accounting report mean nothing, per se, as to economic value.

26
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:15,160
它们只是指引，告诉你该如何去求得经济价值。
They are guidelines to tell you something about how to get at economic value.

27
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:17,780
但它们本身什么也说明不了。
But they don’t tell you anything.

28
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:22,700
财务报表里没有答案，
There are no answers in the financial statements.

29
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:28,800
只有帮助你找到答案的指引。
There are guidelines to enable you to figure out the answer.

30
00:02:28,860 --> 00:02:32,020
而要找到答案，你必须懂一些生意。
And to figure out that answer, you have to understand something about business.

31
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:36,400
你不需要懂很多数学。我是说，数学并不复杂。
You don’t have to understand a lot about mathematics. I mean, the math is not complicated.

32
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:39,540
但你确实必须懂这门生意。
But you do have to understand something about the business.

33
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:42,080
这和你打算买一栋公寓楼时会做的事情一样，
But that’s the same thing you would do if you were going to buy an apartment house,

34
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:47,220
或者买一座农场、任何你感兴趣的小生意。
or a farm, or any other small business you might be interested in.

35
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:49,880
你会设法弄清楚：你现在要付出多少，
You would try to figure out what you are laying out currently,

36
00:02:49,940 --> 00:02:52,300
随着时间推移可能收回多少，
and what you are likely to get back over time,

37
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:54,420
你对收回它有多大把握，
and how certain you felt about getting it,

38
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:56,380
以及它和其他选择相比如何。
and how it compared to other alternatives.

39
00:02:56,440 --> 00:03:01,110
我们做的就是这些，只不过对象是大企业而已。
That’s all we do, we just do it with large businesses, basically.

40
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:07,080
会计数字对我们非常有帮助，
The accounting figures are very helpful to us,

41
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:14,790
因为它们通常会引导我们去思考该思考的东西。
in the sense that they generally guide us to what we should be thinking about.

42
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:22,120
当然，如果我们发现某些数字看起来是有人
And of course, if we find numbers where it looks like people are taking

43
00:03:22,180 --> 00:03:25,940
在会计准则允许的范围内，做了最乐观的解释，
the most optimistic interpretation of things that they can under GAAP and all of that,

44
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:31,520
我们就会非常担心那些看起来在以任何方式粉饰数字的人。
we get very worried about people who look like they massage the numbers in any way.

45
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:34,510
而这样做的人多得是。
And there are plenty of people that do.

46
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:40,860
估值的第一步，并不是挑选折现率。
The first step in valuation is not choosing a discount rate.

47
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:43,648
而是先问自己一个问题：
It is asking yourself one question:

48
00:03:43,708 --> 00:03:51,097
这家企业未来的现金流，能否被有把握地预测在一个区间之内？
can this business’s future cash flows be forecast, with confidence, within a range?

49
00:03:51,157 --> 00:03:58,974
如果不能，就把它放进“太难”的那一堆，价格再诱人，也不必理会。
If not, it goes into the “too hard” pile, however tempting the price.

50
00:03:59,034 --> 00:04:05,204
如果能，再把它的价值，与价格放在一起比较。
If so, only then do you weigh its value against its price.

51
00:04:05,264 --> 00:04:10,132
在巴菲特看来，确定性，比便宜更重要。
For Buffett, certainty matters more than cheapness.
